<article class="env-lemma" id="07R9">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07R9">Lemma <span data-tag="07R9">37.21.3</span>.</a> A smooth morphism is regular. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $f : X \to Y$ be a smooth morphism. As $f$ is locally of finite presentation, see Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01VE" data-tag="01VE">29.35.8</a> the fibres $X_ y$ are locally of finite type over a field, hence locally Noetherian. Moreover, $f$ is flat, see Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01VF" data-tag="01VF">29.35.9</a>. Finally, the fibres $X_ y$ are smooth over a field (by Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01VB" data-tag="01VB">29.35.5</a>) and hence geometrically regular by Varieties, Lemma <a href="/tag/056T" data-tag="056T">33.25.4</a>. Thus $f$ is regular by Lemma <a href="/tag/07R8" data-tag="07R8">37.21.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>